# Nobody has written a type in this file. A list that the front end wrote from use is no word for a guard: what is read under an index may be a list, a view or a text. Where the body itself tells the
# parameter apart it has said that a list is one of several things that come, and has its own way for each: there the guard asks once at the entry for what the turns of the loop would ask again and again.
# Without it every turn asked whether `value` is a list and what `rounds` is, and the sum was kept as a value of any kind: two and a half times the instructions.
# f1 = count, f2 = ends
# RUN: plan units mechanisms=all
# CHECK: unit f1:ParameterGuard {{*}}Array
# RUN(READS): plan units mechanisms=all
# READS-NOT: unit f2:ParameterGuard
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = () => {};
# ANSWERS: 15 6
# ANSWERS: 10 abcd
